# T18303 — Communication Test in Private VLAN - Send from Private port — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-30 — PASS

Verdict: PASS. The objective, "All packets were sent to Uplink port from Private port", held for every
stream sent from a private port: 100/100 reached the uplink, and 0 reached any other private port or the
control port. The two unicast lines that must NOT be delivered were not (112 → 113 and 113 → 112: 0 at
the target), even though both destination MACs were known (static FDB entries). With the private VLAN
off (the same ports in a plain VLAN), the same broadcast and unicast did reach the other private ports,
so the isolation comes from the private VLAN. Run labelled: clean.

How the "forwarded to all ports" wording was read: the expected results say a private port's
broadcast (lines 1 and 5) "should be forwarded to all ports". Read literally ("every port of the
VLAN, other private ports included"), that contradicts lines 3 and 4 (private ports cannot reach each
other) and the case objective. It was therefore graded against the objective: forwarded to every port
a private port can reach, which is the uplink. The measurement for both readings is in the table below.
Under the literal reading, lines 1, 2 and 5 would each fail on the missing private-port copies.

Operator: bench-runner subagent (sentinel = parent session, /test-mode shape A), Terrence away.
Queue: IE520/CAMPAIGN-QUEUE-2026-09-29.md row 7. Case text: ck.db AWPTCM-T18303 (2 steps). Step 1 is
"Setup: Same configuration as AWP-9204" (the T18302 setup), and it ran on the configuration built for
T18302 at 16:45, right after that case's streams.

## Bench mapping and configuration
Identical to 18302.log (read that file for the bench mapping, the configuration, its read-back, the
plain-VLAN baseline and the teardown). In brief: private VLAN primary 3980 + isolated 3981 (case VLAN 10 is the
sa1 transit). Uplink IXIA-111 = port3.0.13 promiscuous (eth1, 0000.0000.0110). Private IXIA-112 =
port1.0.2 (eth3 tag 3991, 0000.0000.0120), IXIA-113 = port1.0.13 (eth2 tag 3993, 0000.0000.0130), IXIA-114 =
port4.0.9 (eth2 tag 3994, 0000.0000.0140). Control port1.0.9 (eth3 tag 3992) is outside the private VLAN. The
case's static ARP entries (vlan3980 192.168.100.254/24, arp .1–.4 on those ports) installed static FDB
entries in 3980 and 3981 (evidence/18302/pv-cfg.out). **Step 1 PASS** (configuration accepted and read
back, no `% ` line).

Pre-case state: as for 18302 (gate 16:15–16:21, probe 2026-09-30T031557Z MATCH, boot configs
tb470-bench.cfg). Gate items 5/7/9 not applicable (hand-driven, skipped).

## Feature-OFF baseline (plain VLAN 3979, 16:43; evidence/18302/pv-b0a.out, pv-b0b.out)
- 113 broadcast → eth1 100, 112 (eth3 3991) 100, 114 (eth2 3994) 100: private-to-be ports reach each other.
- 112 unicast → 0000.0000.0130 → 113 (eth2 3993) 100: known unicast between them is delivered.

## Step 2 — send from the private ports (16:49:31–16:51:30)
Sender vsend.py, 100 frames per stream. Driver evidence/group-2026-09-30/vstep.sh. 112 is driven from
eth3 tagged 3991 (x230 strips it: untagged into DUT port1.0.2); 113 from eth2 tagged 3993; 114 from eth2
tagged 3994. Captures `tcpdump -Q in -e` on eth1, eth2 and eth3 (inbound only, so a sender's own frames
are not counted), filtered on the sender MAC. DUT in/out packet deltas: background is about +10 to +36.

| stream (case) | from → dst | eth1 (uplink 111) | 112 (eth3 3991) | 113 (eth2 3993) | 114 (eth2 3994) | control (eth3 3992) | DUT in (sender port) / out 3.0.13 | expected | result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 Broadcast | 112 → ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff | **100** | (sender) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1.0.2 in +101 / +134 | forwarded (objective: to the uplink) | **PASS** |
| 2 Multicast | 112 → 01:80:c2:01:01:01 | **100** | (sender) | 0 | 0 | 0 | +100 / +133 | forwarded | **PASS** |
| 3 Unicast to 113 | 112 → 0000.0000.0130 | 100 | (sender) | **0** | 0 | 0 | +100 / +133 | not forwarded to IXIA-113 | **PASS** |
| 4 Unicast to 112 | 113 → 0000.0000.0120 | 100 | **0** | (sender) | 0 | 0 | 1.0.13 in +110 / +130 | not forwarded to IXIA-112 | **PASS** |
| 5 Broadcast | 114 → ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff | **100** | 0 | 0 | (sender) | 0 | 4.0.9 in +111 / +136 | forwarded (objective: to the uplink) | **PASS** |
| extra: unicast to the uplink | 112 → 0000.0000.0110 | **100** | (sender) | 0 | 0 | 0 | +101 / +134 | (objective) | PASS, not a case line |
Frames at eth1 arrived untagged (promiscuous access egress). DUT output on the other private ports
stayed at background in every stream: port1.0.13 +20..+23, port4.0.9 +20..+23, port1.0.2 +31..+35.
Raw: evidence/18303/18303-{a.bc112,b.mc112,c.u112to113,d.u113to112,e.bc114,f.u112to111}.out + .pcap.

Observation (not graded): lines 3 and 4 were not dropped. The known unicast between two isolated
hosts was sent to the uplink (100/100 at eth1, port3.0.13 output +133/+130), although its destination
MAC is a static entry on the other host port. So on this platform a private port's traffic goes to
the uplink whatever its destination MAC. That is exactly the case objective ("All packets were sent to
Uplink port from Private port"), and it differs from a lookup-then-block isolation that would drop
it. Recorded so a future case expecting a drop is not surprised.

